WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.220
A scene of falling stars looks amazing

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.900
and we all love to see it !

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.500
What are these falling stars?

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.200
They are meteoroids or similar bodies from space,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.240
which enter the earth’s atmosphere.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.280
However, this wasn’t known to people back in time.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.940
People innocently believed that actual stars from space

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.680
fall down on the earth’s surface.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.960
It was due to advancements in science and technology

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.780
that many discoveries were made, and the fact

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.640
that these are not stars but meteoroids was accepted!

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.020
Same is applicable to many legendary discoveries

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.020
of the past.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.860
Due to several reasons,

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.180
many discoveries were left ignored and unaccepted.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.220
But the advancement in technology

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.280
helped in better research which could support the long

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.980
ignored works of many scientists!

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.060
One example of such unfortunate incidences

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.360
was the work of the father of Genetics, Gregor Mendel !

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.120
Mendel’s work was far beyond excellence!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.600
However, it wasn’t appreciated right from the time

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.940
it was put forth before the scientific society.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.360
Several reasons led to the demotivating rejection

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.520
of his efforts!

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.760
One of the major reasons, included his concept

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.540
of “non-blending” inheritance .

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.460
According to Mendel, genes or FACTORS to be precise,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.880
do not blend and that the phenotype of offsprings

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.240
is similar to only one parent.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.840
It cannot be an intermediate between the two parents.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.660
However, the variations seen in organisms in general

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.720
could not be explained by this concept

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.680
of non-blending of characters!

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.740
Secondly, Mendel introduced mathematical calculations

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.660
to explain biological processes.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.180
He presented results in the form of ratios.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.240
At that time, mathematical forms of biological results

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.200
were not easily accepted.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.980
Hence, his work was largely ignored.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.240
Lastly, when Mendel said that there are factors

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.400
which are passed from one generation to the other,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.920
he had no physical proof of those units.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.480
In the sense, there was no evidence of the

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.500
physical form of the factors that Mendel could present.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.020
So the proposition, that discrete units called FACTORS

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.780
exists, was like a hypothetical theory.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.880
Mendel had no proper evidence

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.100
that such units actually exist.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.120
Due to all these reasons, Mendelian genetics remained

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.620
dormant for several years.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.400
After being almost rejected in the mid 1860’s

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.940
Mendel’s work remained unnoticed until the

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.700
beginning of 20th century.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.680
So what exactly happened in the early 1900s?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.540
Who shined a light on the remarkable contributions

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.460
of Gregor Mendel?

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.900
Let us find that out in the next part!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.960
Microscopes ease the lives of scientists.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.820
However, they are not new inventions.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.800
Microscopes were invented several years ago.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.540
Beginning with simple lenses used to zoom in the

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:36.200
desired structures, today, we have electron microscopes,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.500
which can give us minute details

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.840
of the smallest possible structure!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.660
But the microscopes in the nineteenth century

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.680
were not that advanced.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.560
So minute observations of the living cells

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.780
and the cellular components were not really possible.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.440
In the beginning of the twentieth century,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.560
the advancements in microscopy

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.520
and related techniques helped

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.680
in acute observations of the cell division processes.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:08.500
As a result, cytologists could now figure out structures

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.340
that duplicate and divide during cell division .

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.240
Which structures could these be ?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.440
That’s right !

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.020
Scientists were now able to identify

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.940
and spot chromosomes inside the nucleus.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.400
We now know what chromosomes are

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.540
and how they look.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.840
But it wasn’t known back then.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.900
So the newly found structures inside the cell

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.080
grabbed a lot of attention.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.720
Also, by this time, due to the

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.500
understanding of the chromosomal structures,

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.460
processes like mitosis

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.700
and meiosis were well understood.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.480
During the same time, Mendel’s long ignored

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.160
legendary work started gaining importance

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.700
as many scientists started re-evaluating the results.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.620
There were two scientists, from different parts of the

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:02.640
globe, who simultaneously put forth a few hypotheses.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.320
These hypotheses, became a theory later,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.040
which is what we are going to study now.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.720
Walter Sutton, an American geneticist and physician,

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.200
was working on grasshoppers.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.900
He found that chromosomes occur in pairs

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.000
and during meiosis, separate from one another

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.800
in the gametes formed.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.120
He put forth the assumption that a pair of chromosome

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.440
contains one chromosome from mother

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.320
and one from the father.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.220
The separation of chromosomes during meiosis may be

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.260
the explanation of the Mendelian laws of inheritance.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.300
This is what Sutton hypothesised.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.900
Around the same time, a German biologist named

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.300
Theodor Boveri was working on sea urchins.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.740
He found that in order to have a proper

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:56.240
embryonic development, all the chromosomal pairs

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.300
have to be present in the embryo.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.560
Both these works later were combined to give us a

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.180
single theory which came to be known as the

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:08.440
Boveri-Sutton theory of inheritance.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.860
Now, it is also referred to as the

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.900
“Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance”.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.800
The theory, in simple words stated that

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.400
“individual genes are found at specific locations

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.720
on a particular chromosome.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.860
Also, the pattern of behaviour of the chromosomes

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.420
during meiosis explains us the Mendelian laws,

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:33.240
as to why and how genes are inherited .”

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.380
The theory and thus the laws of genetics

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.040
can be explained well with the help of exactly

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.200
three points or observations !

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:46.500
The first point said that chromosomes come in pairs.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.160
These are now called homologous pairs by us !

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.960
One chromosome from the pair comes from the mother

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.320
while the other from the father.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.400
Isn’t this what even Mendel hypothesised about genes ?

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:05.180
He said that “factors”, now called genes, come in pairs.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.720
One factor of the pair is from the mother

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.840
and the other from the father.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.220
The next point stated

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.420
that the chromosomes from a single pair

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.500
separate from each other during the process of meiosis.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.260
That means, one chromosome

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.460
will be passed to the respective gamete.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.920
This is just the simplest explanation of Mendel’s law

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.020
of segregation.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.580
In the law, Mendel emphasised on the

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.880
separation of factors that is alleles into gametes.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.280
The last observation of the theory states that

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.140
different chromosomes assort into gametes

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.660
independent of each other during meiosis.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.640
This is what even Mendel had said

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:51.240
in his law of independent assortment.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.360
The alleles of the different genes assort

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.560
independent of each other during gamete formation.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.520
This is how the Chromosomal theory of inheritance

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.940
helps us understand

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.020
that the genes are present on chromosomes.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.960
And also that the are the units of heredity !

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.860
This is how the theory supported Mendel’s work

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.740
and was useful in proving the Laws of genetics

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.300
put forth by Mendel.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.380
However,

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:23.820
now the question is how was this theory accepted?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.960
What results were presented to prove this theory right

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.500
and acceptable?

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:32.760
A few years later, another legendary scientist

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.600
named Thomas Hunt Morgan,

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.820
carried out a few experiments on the little fruit fly,

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:41.020
Drosophila melanogaster.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.300
His experiments confirmed Sutton

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.380
and Boveri’s theory further.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.880
With all these,

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:51.060
Mendel’s long ignored work gained recognition

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.960
and the remarkable laws of Genetics were accepted!

